act numerator and completed-renewal denominator fields used to compute the share.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"coherence\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"The draft has runAt 2026-06-28T00:02:42Z, which is after the stated review date of 2026-06-27 and may look like a future-dated trace artifact.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Correct or explain the runAt timestamp so the publication record does not appear to use future context.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"interval\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"The interval is justified from a very small, sparse Arizona sample with observed moves, but it does not state whether skipped monthly observations were unavailable or intentionally excluded.\",\"actionRequested\":\"State that the historical sample is the available inspected first-print points, or include the missing monthly first-print points if they were available and materially affect volatility.\"}],\"optionalSuggestions\":[\"Name the CMS variables for ex parte renewals and completed renewals in the reasoning or resolution rule for auditability.\",\"Make the prior/update arithmetic clearer by distinguishing the 93.3 catalog baseline from the 91.5 latest-value starting point.\",\"Clarify whether the 99.0 upper bound is a calibrated 80% cap or a judgmental cap below the mechanical 100% maximum.\"]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-02-36z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-az-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/draft_stdout.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Arizona Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\",\"question\":\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Arizona state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":93.3,\"ciLow\":85.9,\"ciHigh\":99.0,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-12-15\",\"resolutionSource\":\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to Arizona's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in the CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data first publication. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal numerator divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov; ignore later updated submissions or revisions unless CMS corrects the original row before the same release day ends. The official Medicaid.gov monthly reports page verifies this dataset is updated monthly and showed the latest current release, Preliminary March 2026, last updated June 26, 2026; I did not find a future dated official August 2026 placeholder, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.az.aug_2026\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"AZ 2025-07 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":85.9},{\"label\":\"AZ 2025-09 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":86.5},{\"label\":\"AZ 2025-11 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":93.3},{\"label\":\"AZ 2026-01 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":93.9},{\"label\":\"AZ 2026-02 latest inspected first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":91.5}],\"drivers\":[\"Arizona's recent ex parte renewal share is already near the top of the feasible range\",\"Data-matching coverage and eligibility-system automation support persistence in the low 90s\",\"Renewal cohort mix can still move the state share several percentage points month to month\",\"The upper tail is capped by the 100 percent share boundary while downside remains operationally plausible\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360?conditions%5B0%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bproperty%5D=reporting_period&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=202602&conditions%5B1%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bproperty%5D=preliminary_or_updated&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bvalue%5D=P\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-28T00:02:42Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Arizona Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a state row, not a national weighted average: Arizona's original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local catalog entry for the Arizona August 2026 ex parte renewal share resolver.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior catalog point 93.3, prior 80% interval 85.9 to 99.0, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.az.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the official Medicaid.gov monthly reports page to verify the release vehicle and current update cadence evidence.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official page evidence: the page says data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly; it listed Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data with Last Updated June 26, 2026, plus February 2026 preliminary and updated entries also Last Updated June 26, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS Medicaid eligibility processing dataset identifiers and resolver notes used for this target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched ledger dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, CMS datastore id 6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360 in the local CMS Medicaid guidance, and expected publication lag of about 3 to 4 months after the reporting period.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched recent Arizona ex parte renewal-share reference points from the official-source-derived forecast catalog context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Arizona values: 2025-07 = 85.9 percent, 2025-09 = 86.5 percent, 2025-11 = 93.3 percent, 2026-01 = 93.9 percent, and 2026-02 = 91.5 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the latest available Arizona point and recent dispersion around it for a first-print August 2026 projection.\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest inspected Arizona value 2026-02 = 91.5 percent; 2025-07 to 2025-09 change was +0.6 percentage points, 2025-09 to 2025-11 change was +6.8 percentage points, 2025-11 to 2026-01 change was +0.6 percentage points, and 2026-01 to 2026-02 change was -2.4 percentage points.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the most relevant outside view is Arizona's own post-unwinding first-print run from July 2025 through February 2026. It shifted from the mid-80s into the low-90s, with the latest three observed points centered near 92.9 percent, so a persistence-plus-small-trend prior dominates a broad national average.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: the level is high and plausibly reflects mature data matching rather than a temporary spike, but the February dip from 93.9 to 91.5 argues against extrapolating rapidly toward 100. The upper bound is mechanically capped, while downside comes from manual-heavy cohorts or data-source interruptions.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Arizona latest-value persistence with a damped local trend, using the July 2025, September 2025, November 2025, January 2026, and February 2026 official-source-derived sample. Prior catalog baseline was 93.3, and I leave it unchanged because the latest 91.5 is below the January high but the November-January plateau supports recovery; adjustment components are +1.0 pp for high recent plateau, +0.8 pp for longer-run improvement from 85.9 to 91.5, and 0.0 pp for capped upside after starting from 91.5. The 80% interval uses realized first-print moves up to 6.8 pp, widened for six-month cohort and system risk, then capped near 99.0 because 100 percent is the natural maximum.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: upside outside the interval is hard because it would require Arizona to print essentially universal ex parte renewals near 100 percent. Downside outside the interval would require a renewal cohort with unusually poor electronic match rates, a state eligibility-system problem, or a CMS reporting break that pulls the share below the mid-80s.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point calculation: latest observed 91.5 percent plus +1.0 pp for the November-January high plateau and +0.8 pp for the broader July-February improvement gives 93.3 percent. Interval calculation: lower bound 93.3 - 7.4 = 85.9; upper bound is 93.3 + 5.7 = 99.0 after applying the 100 percent cap and rounding to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verified the monthly release vehicle and current June 26, 2026 update, but did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":93.3,\"ciLow\":85.9,\"ciHigh\":99.0}]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-02-36z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-az-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting