aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:6:- series: cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.al.aug_2026\\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-57-39z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-al-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:13:- catalogSlug: \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\"\\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-57-39z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-al-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:15:- dataPointId: \\\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.al.aug_2026\\\"\\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-57-39z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-al-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:18:- resolutionRule: \\\"Resolves to Alabama's ex parte renewal share for the August 2026 reporting period, computed from the original (O) submission row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes it (expected roughly three to four months after the period). Numerator and denominator as published; share computed to one decimal.\\\"\\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-57-39z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-al-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:50:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"US\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Alabama Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Alabama state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":57.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":51.9,\\\"ciHigh\\\":62.2,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-12-15\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to Alabama's August 2026 reporting-period original first-publication state row in the CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data on data.medicaid.gov. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal count divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available through the dataset; ignore later updated submissions or revisions unless CMS corrects the original row before the same release day ends. The registered ledger resolution date is 2026-12-15; I did not find a future-dated CMS release-calendar placeholder in this fast run, so this remains tied to the canonical target while the reasoning notes the schedule evidence limitation.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.al.aug_2026\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"AL 2025-07 original first-print ex parte renewal share\\\",\\\"value\\\":51.6},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"AL 2025-09 original first-print ex parte renewal share\\\",\\\"value\\\":54.1},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"AL 2025-11 original first-print ex parte renewal share\\\",\\\"value\\\":55.8},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"AL 2026-01 original first-print ex parte renewal share\\\",\\\"value\\\":58.3},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"AL 2026-02 latest inspected original first-print ex parte renewal share\\\",\\\"value\\\":56.0}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"Alabama's recent first-print series is clustered in the mid-to-high 50s\\\",\\\"Ex parte performance depends on wage, SNAP, vital-records, and other data-match coverage\\\",\\\"Eligibility-system and vendor changes tend to create step changes rather than smooth monthly trend\\\",\\\"Renewal cohort composition can move the numerator and denominator month to month\\\",\\\"CMS renewal-policy compliance pressure supports persistence near recent post-unwinding levels\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data\\\",\\\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\\\",\\\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/program-information/medicaid-and-chip-enrollment-data/report-highlights\\\",\\\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-27T23:57:54Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Forecast for Alabama Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is a state row, not a national weighted average: Alabama's original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Medicaid.gov Medicaid & CHIP Enrollment Data page for reporting vehicle and public-release framing.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched CMS statement that all 50 states and DC provide data each month on application, eligibility, and enrollment processes; the page listed March 2026 data highlights and 3 related report/data links.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Medicaid.gov monthly application, eligibility determination, and enrollment reports page for latest dated release evidence.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched monthly page evidence: Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data was Last Updated June 26, 2026; Updated February 2026 and Preliminary February 2026 entries were also Last Updated June 26, 2026; the page states data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Medicaid.gov March 2026 data highlights page for current official release lag and national reporting context.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched March 2026 highlight values: 74,294,361 people enrolled in Medicaid and CHIP, 67,080,865 in Medicaid, 7,213,496 in CHIP, and the map data were last updated June 26, 2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"repo.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Inspected the local forecast catalog and target registry for the canonical Alabama August 2026 ex parte renewal-share target.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior point 57.1, prior 80% interval 51.9 to 62.2, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.al.aug_2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"repo.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Read the local official-source-derived Alabama historical context for this CMS series.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched Alabama original first-print values: 2025-07 = 51.6 percent, 2025-09 = 54.1 percent, 2025-11 = 55.8 percent, 2026-01 = 58.3 percent, and 2026-02 = 56.0 percent.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference class: the most relevant outside view is Alabama's own post-unwinding original first-print run from July 2025 through February 2026, centered around 55.2 percent across the five inspected points and with a latest value of 56.0 percent. I use Alabama persistence rather than a national average because this resolves one state row.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: the level is mid-to-high 50s; momentum from July 2025 to January 2026 was positive but February slipped to 56.0; one-off monthly cohort composition can move both completed-renewal and ex parte counts; the policy mechanism is continued CMS pressure for ex parte renewals but no known Alabama-specific automation shock in the checked context.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is latest-value persistence with a damped local trend, using the observed official-source-derived sample 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. The update adds +1.0 pp for the 2025-to-early-2026 improvement signal and +0.1 pp for CMS compliance pressure, partly offset by the February dip, moving 56.0 to 57.1. The 80% interval uses realized first-print swings in this Alabama sample, then widens for cohort mix and missing-month uncertainty.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: upside outside the interval would require a sustained automation or data-match improvement pushing Alabama above roughly 62 percent. Downside outside the interval would require a manual-heavy renewal cohort, data-source outage, or operational regression pushing the share below roughly 52 percent. A schedule counter-consideration is that CMS publishes this series monthly but I did not verify a CMS page explicitly naming 2026-12-15 for the August 2026 first print.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"textkup\",\"call\":\"Read the current BLS Employment Situation Summary for May 2026.\",\"result\":\"BLS reported total nonfarm payroll employment increased by 172,000 in May and the unemployment rate was unchanged at 4.3 percent; unemployed people were 7.3 million.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read BLS archived May 2026 Employment Situation table A-1 for recent household-survey values.\",\"result\":\"Seasonally adjusted unemployment rates in table A-1 were Jan 2026 4.3, Feb 2026 4.4, Mar 2026 4.3, Apr 2026 4.3, May 2026 4.3 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"history.mirror\",\"call\":\"Checked FRED UNRATE as a history mirror for recent BLS CPS values and next-release metadata.\",\"result\":\"FRED showed May 2026 4.3, Apr 2026 4.3, Mar 2026 4.3, Feb 2026 4.4, Jan 2026 4.3, updated Jun 5, 2026, with next release date Jul 2, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference class: one-month moves in the rounded unemployment rate are usually small, and the immediate recent reference class is especially persistent: five latest monthly values are all between 4.3 and 4.4, with four of five at 4.3.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The main downside risk is continued strong labor demand: May payrolls rose 172,000, participation was steady at 61.8 percent, and the unemployment rate has held at 4.3 despite month-to-month changes in unemployment levels.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Use persistence as the anchor: median of Jan-May rounded rates = 4.3. Apply no drift because May payrolls were strong and participation was flat, but widen the 80 percent interval to roughly one BLS household-survey rounded-rate move below and above: 4.1 to 4.6.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":4.3,\"ciLow\":4.1,\"ciHigh\":4.6}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/parsed_cells.json:32:        \"label\": \"Jan 2026\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/parsed_cells.json:82:        \"result\": \"Fetched W823RC1 latest values: Apr 2026 1643.7, Mar 2026 1636.9, Feb 2026 1628.6, Jan 2026 1623.2; units are billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted annual rate.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-09-00z-statjp-lfs-unemployment-rate-2026-05/normalized_cells.json:80:    \"result\": \"FRED series LRUNTTTTJPM156S shows Apr 2026 2.5 percent, Mar 2026 2.7 percent, Feb 2026 2.6 percent, Jan 2026 2.7 percent, and Dec 2025 2.6 percent; units are percent, seasonally adjusted, monthly.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/normalized_cells.json:32:    \"label\": \"Jan 2026\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/normalized_cells.json:82:    \"result\": \"Fetched W823RC1 latest values: Apr 2026 1643.7, Mar 2026 1636.9, Feb 2026 1628.6, Jan 2026 1623.2; units are billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted annual rate.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/normalized_cells.json:79:    \"result\": \"Seasonally adjusted unemployment rates in table A-1 were Jan 2026 4.3, Feb 2026 4.4, Mar 2026 4.3, Apr 2026 4.3, May 2026 4.3 percent.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/normalized_cells.json:85:    \"result\": \"FRED showed May 2026 4.3, Apr 2026 4.3, Mar 2026 4.3, Feb 2026 4.4, Jan 2026 4.3, updated Jun 5, 2026, with next release date Jul 2, 2026.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/cells.with_activity.json:32:        \"label\": \"Jan 2026\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-27-13z-bea-government-social-benefits-social-security-2026-05/cells.with_activity.json:82:        \"result\": \"Fetched W823RC1 latest values: Apr 2026 1643.7, Mar 2026 1636.9, Feb 2026 1628.6, Jan 2026 1623.2; units are billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted annual rate.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-09-00z-statjp-lfs-unemployment-rate-2026-05/stderr.txt:182:{\"slug\":\"japan-lfs-unemployment-rate-2026-05\",\"country\":\"JP\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Japan unemployment rate, May 2026\",\"question\":\"Statistics Bureau of Japan Labour Force Survey Basic Tabulation unemployment rate, total persons aged 15 years or over, seasonally adjusted, May 2026, first print\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":2.5,\"ciLow\":2.3,\"ciHigh\":2.8,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-06-30\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Official agency release\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.stat.go.jp/english/data/roudou/result.html\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the first Statistics Bureau of Japan Labour Force Survey Basic Tabulation May 2026 seasonally adjusted unemployment rate for total persons aged 15 years or over, as first released on the official monthly results/survey results page on June 30, 2026. Use the agency's published percent value rounded to one decimal place; ignore later revisions or historical-data back revisions for this forecast cell.\",\"dataPointId\":\"statjp.lfs.unemployment_rate.sa.2026-05.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"2026-04\",\"value\":2.5},{\"label\":\"2026-03\",\"value\":2.7},{\"label\":\"2026-02\",\"value\":2.6},{\"label\":\"2026-01\",\"value\":2.7},{\"label\":\"2025-12\",\"value\":2.6}],\"drivers\":[\"Recent unemployment has stayed in a narrow 2.5-2.7 percent range\",\"April 2026 latest value was 2.5 percent\",\"Japan labor market changes are usually gradual month to month\",\"One-month forecast horizon limits macro information gain\",\"Seasonal adjustment revisions occurred with January 2026 release\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.stat.go.jp/english/data/roudou/index.html\",\"https://www.stat.go.jp/english/data/roudou/1543.html\",\"https://www.stat.go.jp/english/data/roudou/result.html\",\"https://www.e-stat.go.jp/en/stat-search/files?cycle=0&tclass=000001226526\",\"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/LRUNTTTTJPM156S\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-17T02:09:06Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast Japan May 2026 LFS unemployment rate\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is the Statistics Bureau of Japan Labour Force Survey Basic Tabulation, seasonally adjusted unemployment rate for total persons aged 15 years or over, May 2026 first print, not a later revised e-Stat historical value.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the Statistics Bureau Labour Force Survey landing and survey-results pages for the official series surface and latest monthly release status.\",\"result\":\"The official page says fiscal 2026 release schedule was published on 2026-01-30; the survey-results page lists April 2026 monthly Basic Tabulation released on 2026-05-29; e-Stat table 1-a-1 covers major items including Unemployment rate, survey date 2026Apr, update date 2026-05-29, since Jan. 1953.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.calendar\",\"call\":\"Checked the Statistics Bureau Labour Force Survey release schedule for the May 2026 reference month.\",\"result\":\"The official schedule lists Basic Tabulation reference month 2026 May with date of release June 30; nearby monthly dates include April May 29, June July 31, July August 28, and August October 2.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"mirror.history\",\"call\":\"Checked FRED/OECD monthly seasonally adjusted Japan unemployment-rate history as a history mirror only, not as the final resolution source.\",\"result\":\"FRED series LRUNTTTTJPM156S shows Apr 2026 2.5 percent, Mar 2026 2.7 percent, Feb 2026 2.6 percent, Jan 2026 2.7 percent, and Dec 2025 2.6 percent; units are percent, seasonally adjusted, monthly.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class: over the last five fetched monthly observations, the mean is 2.62 percent and every value lies between 2.5 and 2.7 percent, so the best prior for one month ahead is persistence near 2.6 with low volatility.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Use a persistence-weighted estimate: 60 percent on April 2026 at 2.5 and 40 percent on the recent five-month mean 2.62 gives 0.6*2.5 + 0.4*2.62 = 2.548, rounded to the agency precision as 2.5 percent. Set an 80 percent interval around recent monthly variation and one-print risk at 2.3 to 2.8 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",