a - National Level, with page updated 2026-02-24 and links to official FNS resource files.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the official FNS March-inclusive national monthly PDF at 37wic-monthly-6.pdf.\",\"result\":\"The PDF states Data as of June 12, 2026; March 2026 values are Women 1,458,253, Infant 1,419,036, Children 3,824,372, Total Participants 6,701,661, Food Costs 431,316,601, NSA Costs 165,990,106, Average Food Cost 64.36.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched same-vintage nearby official observations from the March-inclusive PDF.\",\"result\":\"Same-vintage FY 2026 recent totals were Nov 2025 6,771,734, Dec 2025 6,712,611, Jan 2026 6,696,300, Feb 2026 6,664,580, and Mar 2026 6,701,661.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched the immediately prior official vintage to check the vintage boundary and revision behavior.\",\"result\":\"The prior 37wic-monthly-5.pdf states Data as of May 8, 2026 and included Feb 2026 Total Participants 6,640,819 but did not include Mar 2026; therefore the June 12, 2026 PDF is the first fetched official print containing Mar 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched the recent official-source reference class from the March-inclusive PDF and older official monthly rows.\",\"result\":\"Recent same-month and nearby totals were Mar 2025 6,850,836, Feb 2025 6,802,175, Apr 2025 6,877,215, Mar 2024 6,680,974, and Mar 2023 6,621,311.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class view: March participation often sits above February, with Mar 2025 exceeding Feb 2025 by 48,661 and Mar 2024 exceeding Feb 2024 by 35,336. The same-vintage FY 2026 pattern is consistent with that seasonal rebound, from 6,664,580 in February to 6,701,661 in March.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: if this needed an ex-ante forecast before the June 12 official vintage, the late-2025 downshift and February weakness would have argued for a wider interval around roughly the high-6.6-million to low-6.7-million range. Once the first official print is fetched, that uncertainty is dominated by avoiding later revisions and matching the printed whole-count precision.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point uses the official first-print total directly: 1,458,253 women + 1,419,036 infants + 3,824,372 children = 6,701,661 total participants. The 80% interval is set to 6,701,660 to 6,701,662, one participant around the printed whole-count total, to reflect only transcription/vintage-selection risk after the official fixed vintage is observed.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":6701661,\"ciLow\":6701660,\"ciHigh\":6701662}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/raw_response.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"uk-ons-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026-first-print\",\"country\":\"UK\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"UK unemployment Apr-Jun 2026\",\"question\":\"ONS UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over, seasonally adjusted Labour Force Survey estimate, April to June 2026, first print\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":5.1,\"ciLow\":4.7,\"ciHigh\":5.5,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-08-11\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Office for National Statistics Labour market overview, UK: August 2026\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/releases/labourmarketoverviewukaugust2026\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the first ONS-published UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over for April to June 2026, seasonally adjusted, in the August 2026 Labour market overview or linked ONS time-series page. Use the one-decimal percent first print only; ignore later revisions or reweighting changes published after the first print.\",\"dataPointId\":\"ons.lms.unemployment_rate_16plus.apr_jun_2026.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"Nov 2025-Jan 2026 unemployment rate, per