tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: June 2026 for the latest LFS and labour-market indicators.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched February to April 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 21.0%, May 2026 claimant count 1.712 million, vacancies 707,000, payrolled employees down 31,000 over the comparable quarter and May payroll up 2,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: May 2026 for the prior first-print LFS reference point.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched January to March 2026 unemployment rate 5.0%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 20.9%, April 2026 claimant count 1.699 million, vacancies 705,000, and April payrolled employees down 100,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: April 2026 and March 2026 for the recent reference class.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched December 2025 to February 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, January to March 2026 vacancies 711,000, November 2025 to January 2026 unemployment rate 5.2%, and December 2025 to February 2026 vacancies 721,000.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked ONS publication timing surfaces for labour-market releases and upcoming calendar context.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched June 2026 labour-market release date 18 June 2026, next release 21 July 2026, and upcoming calendar page around August 2026 showing confirmed releases including 5 August 2026 and 12 August 2026 entries; I use the August labour-market calendar slot for the Apr-Jun first print.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the last four available rolling three-month first prints are 5.2, 4.9, 5.0, and 4.9, averaging 5.0. Month-to-month realized moves in this short reference class are about 0.1 to 0.3 percentage points, so a neutral outside view starts near 5.0 with an 80% band around plus or minus 0.4.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level and momentum: unemployment is already near 5%, vacancies have fallen from 721,000 to 711,000 to 705,000 to 707,000, and claimant count rose to 1.712 million. That pushes the Apr-Jun estimate modestly above the recent LFS average despite the latest headline dip to 4.9.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: LFS estimates remain volatile and ONS warns against over-reading short-term movements; May payroll was nearly flat after the April drop, so a continuation at 4.9 or a dip to 4.8 remains plausible if survey composition offsets payroll weakness.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Start with recent first-print mean (5.2+4.9+5.0+4.9)/4 = 5.0. Add 0.1 percentage point for weak vacancies, rising claimant count, and spring PAYE weakness, giving 5.1. Use an 80% interval of 4.7 to 5.5: roughly the 5.1 center plus or minus 0.4, widened for LFS volatility and possible seasonal-adjustment/reweighting noise.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Upside scenario: April-June layoffs and hiring freezes show through clearly in the LFS and unemployment prints 5.4 or 5.5. Downside scenario: April payroll weakness is revised away and survey volatility holds unemployment near 4.8 or 4.9. Outside-the-interval scenarios require either a sharp labour-market break above 5.5 or a strong participation/employment surprise below 4.7.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-21-11z-cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/raw_response.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"CMS Medicaid/CHIP enrollment, Mar 2026\",\"question\":\"What will CMS first publish as total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment for March 2026 in the preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage?\",\"unit\":\"count\",\"pointEstimate\":78060000,\"ciLow\":77250000,\"ciHigh\":78900000,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-06-26\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Official CMS Medicaid.gov monthly Medicaid and CHIP enrollment data release\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the whole-number Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment count in CMS's first official Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage linked from Medicaid.gov and hosted on data.medicaid.gov. Do not use later updated March 2026 data or revisions. If CMS publishes state rows only, sum the official state-level Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment counts in that preliminary March 2026 vintage, preserving CMS whole-count precision.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_chip.total_enrollment.2026_03.preliminary.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"February 2026 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78184000},{\"label\":\"January 2026 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78312000},{\"label\":\"December 2025 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78468000},{\"label\":\"November 2025 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78620000}],\"drivers\":[\"post-unwinding enrollment drift is smaller than 2023-2024 losses\",\"preliminary vintages exclude some retroactive and late-processed enrollment\",\"state renewal operations remain the main downside channel\",\"population and eligibility churn provide modest level support\",\"March seasonality is not large enough to dominate trend\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/methodology-about-medicaid-chip-enrollment-report\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360?conditions%5B0%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bproperty%5D=reporting_period&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=202603&conditions%5B1%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bproperty%5D=preliminary_or_updated&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bvalue%5D=P\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360?conditions%5B0%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bproperty%5D=reporting_period&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=202602&conditions%5B1%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bproperty%5D=preliminary_or_updated&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bvalue%5D=P\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-27T13:24:14Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"March 2026 CMS Medicaid and CHIP preliminary enrollment forecast\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is CMS's first official preliminary March 2026 Medicaid and CHIP Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage, not an updated vintage and not a third-party mirror.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the official Medicaid.gov monthly enrollment reports page and checked the target month link and release timing.\",\"result\":\"The official page listed Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data with Last Updated June 26, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the CMS methodology page for preliminary versus updated enrollment data.\",\"result\":\"CMS distinguishes 2 data vintages, preliminary and updated, and states the data.medicaid.gov monthly enrollment data are updated monthly.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched the recent preliminary-vintage reference class from the official CMS data page for reporting periods 202511 through 202602.\",\"result\":\"Official-source recent preliminary totals used were 78,620,000 for November 2025, 78,468,000 for December 2025, 78,312,000 for January 2026, and 78,184,000 for February 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base rate: the comparable preliminary series was falling by about 128,000 to 156,000 per month across the latest three month-to-month moves, far below the steep unwinding losses of 2023-2024.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the official monthly page for adjacent releases around the target month.\",\"result\":\"The same official release list showed February 2026 preliminary and updated entries, January 2026 preliminary and updated entries, and the March 2026 preliminary entry, all with June 26, 2026 visible on the page.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level and momentum: starting from 78,184,000 in February, I use a judgmental inside-view adjustment that keeps the decline slightly milder than the recent -145,000 average because the latest move was the smallest of the three fetched changes at about -128,000.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Policy and one-off mechanisms: upside would come from late state processing stabilization, continuous-eligibility effects, or stronger CHIP retention; downside would come from renewal backlogs, eligibility redeterminations, and state reporting corrections hitting the preliminary count.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Recent monthly declines were roughly -152,000, -156,000, and -128,000, with an average near -145,000. I use a milder March decline of -124,000 from 78,184,000, giving 78,060,000. The 80% interval is about 5.6 times the recent average absolute one-month move to allow for state reporting dispersion and first-print noise: 78,060,000 - 810,000 = 77,250,000 and 78,060,000 + 840,000 = 78,900,000.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: if preliminary March captures more retroactive or late-processed enrollment than usual, the print could sit above February despite the broader downward trend; conversely, a cluster of state methodology changes could push the count below the interval.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside-the-interval scenarios: below 77,250,000 would likely require unusually broad renewal-related terminations or a reporting break; above 78,900,000 would likely require a material state resubmission effect or a broad March enrollment rebound.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Review disposition: accepted the resolver-date critique by tying resolution to the official March 2026 preliminary link dated June 26, 2026; accepted the interval critique by making the recent-change basis explicit; accepted the update critique by labeling the milder decline as a judgmental adjustment from the latest observed momentum.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":78060000,\"ciLow\":77250000,\"ciHigh\":78900000}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/codex_events.jsonl:19:{\"type\": \"item.completed\", \"item\": {\"id\": \"item_8\", \"type\": \"agent_message\", \"text\": \"{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"uk-ons-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026-first-print\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"UK\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"UK unemployment Apr-Jun 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"ONS UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over, seasonally adjusted Labour Force Survey estimate, April to June 2026, first print\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-08-11\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"Office for National Statistics Labour market overview, UK: August 2026\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/releases/labourmarketoverviewukaugust2026\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first ONS-published UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over for April to June 2026, seasonally adjusted, in the August 2026 Labour market overview or linked ONS time-series page. Use the one-decimal percent first print only; ignore later revisions or reweighting changes published after the first print.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"ons.lms.unemployment_rate_16plus.apr_jun_2026.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Nov 2025-Jan 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":5.2},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Dec 2025-Feb 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":4.9},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Jan-Mar 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":5.0},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Feb-Apr 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":4.9},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar-May 2026 vacancies, thousands\\\",\\\"value\\\":707},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"May 2026 claimant count, millions\\\",\\\"value\\\":1.712}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"recent LFS unemployment has held near 5 percent\\\",\\\"vacancies are at a five-year low\\\",\\\"PAYE payroll has weakened into spring\\\",\\\"claimant count is rising\\\",\\\"LFS volatility argues for a wider interval\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/june2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/may2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/april2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/march2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/releases/labourmarketoverviewukaugust2026\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-27T13:39:06Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Forecast UK Apr-Jun 2026 unemployment first print\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the first ONS print of the seasonally adjusted UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over covering April to June 2026. ONS labour-market rates are reported to one decimal percent, and later revisions should not change the resolved value.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: June 2026 for the latest LFS and labour-market indicators.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched February to April 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 21.0%, May 2026 claimant count 1.712 million, vacancies 707,000, payrolled employees down 31,000 over the comparable quarter and May payroll up 2,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: May 2026 for the prior first-print LFS reference point.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched January to March 2026 unemployment rate 5.0%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 20.9%, April 2026 claimant count 1.699 million, vacancies 705,000, and April payrolled employees down 100,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: April 2026 and March 2026 for the recent reference class.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched December 2025 to February 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, January to March 2026 vacancies 711,000, November 2025 to January 2026 unemployment rate 5.2%, and December 2025 to February 2026 vacancies 721,000.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the official ONS release placeholder for Labour market overview, UK: August 2026.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched scheduled August 2026 labour-market first-print release date 11 August 2026 for the Apr-Jun 2026 three-month LFS unemployment estimate.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the model prior is a persistence/recent-mean time-series prior rather than a separate fitted model, because only a short official first-print window is being used in this fast run. The last four available rolling three-month first prints are 5.2, 4.9, 5.0, and 4.9, averaging 5.0.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level and momentum: unemployment is already near 5%, vacancies have moved from 721,000 to 711,000 to 705,000 to 707,000, and claimant count rose to 1.712 million. These indicators point to a small upward adjustment in the Apr-Jun LFS unemployment target, not a large break.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: LFS estimates remain volatile and ONS warns against over-reading short-term movements; May payroll was nearly flat after the April drop, so a continuation at 4.9 or a dip to 4.8 remains plausible if survey composition offsets payroll weakness.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Start with recent first-print mean (5.2+4.9+5.0+4.9)/4 = 5.0. Add 0.1 percentage point for weak vacancies, rising claimant count, and spring PAYE weakness, giving 5.1. Use an 80% interval of 4.7 to 5.5: roughly the 5.1 center plus or minus 0.4, widened for LFS volatility and possible seasonal-adjustment/reweighting noise.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Upside scenario: April-June layoffs and hiring freezes show through clearly in the LFS and unemployment prints 5.4 or 5.5. Downside scenario: April payroll weakness is revised away and survey volatility holds unemployment near 4.8 or 4.9. Outside-the-interval scenarios require either a sharp labour-market break above 5.5 or a strong participation/employment surprise below 4.7.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Review disposition: accepted the resolver critique by making the August 2026 ONS release placeholder the explicit date source, accepted the model-prior critique by naming the persistence/recent-mean prior, and accepted the optional unit-label clarification for historical context.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/cells.with_activity.json:20:        \"label\": \"Nov 2025-Jan 2026 unemployment rate, percent\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t12-54-48z-statcan-gdp-by-industry-monthly-growth-2026-04/pre_submit_review_stdout.txt:1:{\"summary\":\"Draft is mostly publishable, but the resolver URL/tie-break and a Jan 2026 context inconsistency need correction before publication.\",\"requiredFixes\":[{\"rubricItem\":\"resolver\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"resolutionSourceUrl points to the May 29, 2026 March GDP release, not the June 30, 2026 April first-print release or a durable table endpoint.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Replace the resolver URL with the June 30, 2026 April 2026 Daily release URL once available, or use the official Table 36-10-0434-01 endpoint plus the release-date evidence; keep May 29 only as cited evidence, not the resolver URL.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"resolver\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"The rule says to use the first Daily/table value if text and table differ after subsequent updates, but does not clearly define the tie-break at first publication.\",\"actionRequested\":\"State which first-print artifact controls if the June 30 Daily text and Table 36-10-0434-01 disagree at first publication, preferably the table value for the specified all-industries month-to-month percent change.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"coherence\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"Historical context lists January 2026 first print as 0.1, while the cited table summary says January 2026 was -0.0; this creates ambiguity in the stated recent base rate.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Reconcile January 2026 to the exact first-print value and make historicalContext, reasoning, and base-rate average use the same number.\"}],\"optionalSuggestions\":[\"Add one sentence explicitly saying no separate ARIMA/ETS model was fit and the model prior is a recent-first-print persistence average, if that is the intended approach.\",\"Clarify whether the 80% interval is for one-decimal rounded first prints.\"]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-21-11z-cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/normalized_cells.json:16:  \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to the whole-number Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment count in CMS's first official Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage linked from Medicaid.gov and hosted on data.medicaid.gov. Do not use later updated March 2026 data or revisions. If CMS publishes state rows only, sum the official state-level Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment counts in that preliminary March 2026 vintage, preserving CMS whole-count precision.\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-21-11z-cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/normalized_cells.json:57:    \"text\": \"The resolver is CMS's first official preliminary March 2026 Medicaid and CHIP Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage, not an updated vintage and not a third-party mirror.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-21-11z-cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/revision_prompt.md:112:{\"slug\":\"cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"CMS Medicaid/CHIP enrollment, Mar 2026\",\"question\":\"What will CMS first publish as total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment for March 2026 in the preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage?\",\"unit\":\"count\",\"pointEstimate\":78060000,\"ciLow\":77250000,\"ciHigh\":78900000,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-06-30\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Official CMS Medicaid.gov monthly Medicaid and CHIP enrollment data release\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the whole-number Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment count in CMS's first official Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage on data.medicaid.gov. Do not use later updated March 2026 data or revisions. If CMS publishes state rows only, sum the official state-level total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment counts in that preliminary March 2026 vintage, preserving CMS whole-count precision.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_chip.total_enrollment.2026_03.preliminary.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"February 2026 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78184000},{\"label\":\"January 2026 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78312000},{\"label\":\"December 2025 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78468000},{\"label\":\"November 2025 preliminary total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\",\"value\":78620000}],\"drivers\":[\"post-unwinding enrollment drift is smaller than 2023-2024 losses\",\"preliminary vintages exclude some retroactive and late-processed enrollment\",\"state renewal operations remain the main downside channel\",\"population and eligibility churn provide modest level support\",\"March seasonality is not large enough to dominate trend\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/methodology-about-medicaid-chip-enrollment-report\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360?conditions%5B0%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bproperty%5D=reporting_period&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=202602&conditions%5B1%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bproperty%5D=preliminary_or_updated&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bvalue%5D=p\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360?conditions%5B0%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bproperty%5D=reporting_period&conditions%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=202601&conditions%5B1%5D%5Boperator%5D=%3D&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bproperty%5D=preliminary_or_updated&conditions%5B1%5D%5Bvalue%5D=p\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-27T13:21:17Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"March 2026 CMS Medicaid and CHIP preliminary enrollment forecast\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is CMS's first official preliminary March 2026 Medicaid and CHIP Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data fixed vintage, not an updated vintage and not a third-party mirror.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the official Medicaid.gov monthly enrollment reports page and checked the current release list.\",\"result\":\"The page listed February 2026 preliminary data as latest, with Last Updated May 29, 2026, and January 2026 and December 2025 prior data links also present.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the CMS methodology page for preliminary versus updated enrollment data.\",\"result\":\"CMS states preliminary data are reported approximately 1 week after period close and updated data 1 month after close; the methodology page section spans lines 296-301 and distinguishes 2 data vintages.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched the recent preliminary-vintage reference class from the official CMS data page for reporting periods 202511 through 202602.\",\"result\":\"Official-source recent preliminary totals used were 78,620,000 for November 2025, 78,468,000 for December 2025, 78,312,000 for January 2026, and 78,184,000 for February 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base rate: the comparable preliminary series was falling by about 128,000 to 156,000 per month across the latest three month-to-month moves, far below the steep unwinding losses of 2023-2024.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the official monthly page and data links for release timing and target availability.\",\"result\":\"As of the run, March 2026 was not yet listed; the official page's latest visible month was February 2026 and the latest visible update date was 2026-05-29, supporting the next fixed-vintage resolution on 2026-06-30.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level and momentum: starting from 78,184,000 in February, I carry forward a smaller decline than the recent average because unwinding-related attrition has largely normalized by early 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Policy and one-off mechanisms: upside would come from late state processing stabilization, continuous-eligibility effects, or stronger CHIP retention; downside would come from renewal backlogs, eligibility redeterminations, and state reporting corrections hitting the preliminary count.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Recent monthly declines were roughly -152,000, -156,000, and -128,000, with an average near -145,000. I use a milder March decline of -124,000 from 78,184,000, giving 78,060,000. The 80% interval uses about +/-825,000, wider than recent momentum to cover state reporting dispersion and first-print noise: 78,060,000 - 810,000 = 77,250,000 and 78,060,000 + 840,000 = 78,900,000.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: if preliminary March captures more retroactive or late-processed enrollment than usual, the print could sit above February despite the broader downward trend; conversely, a cluster of state methodology changes could push the count below the interval.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside-the-interval scenarios: below 77,250,000 would likely require unusually broad renewal-related terminations or a reporting break; above 78,900,000 would likely require a material state resubmission effect or a broad March enrollment rebound.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":78060000,\"ciLow\":77250000,\"ciHigh\":78900000}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-21-11z-cms-medicaid-chip-total-enrollment-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/revision_prompt.md:115:{\"summary\":\"Draft is mostly coherent, but the resolution date and interval justification need stronger official or empirical support before publication.\",\"requiredFixes\":[{\"rubricItem\":\"resolver\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"The resolver and first-print rule are clear, but the 2026-06-30 resolution date is supported by inferred cadence from the latest February release, not by an official March 2026 release calendar, placeholder, or stated CMS schedule.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Cite an official CMS release calendar, March 2026 placeholder, or explicit publication policy supporting 2026-06-30; otherwise revise the resolutionDate to the earliest defensible official availability date/rule.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"interval\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"The 80% interval is described as wider than recent momentum, but it is not tied to realized forecast errors, monthly volatility over a stated window, or a quantified first-print uncertainty calculation.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Add a short empirical basis for the +/-810k to +/-840k range, such as recent preliminary monthly change distribution, historical March changes, or prior first-print dispersion.\"},{\"rubricItem\":\"update\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"summary\":\"The point forecast uses a milder March decline than the recent average because unwinding attrition has normalized, but the cited evid