13496},{\"label\":\"March 2026 child Medicaid plus CHIP enrollment, millions\",\"value\":35.571626}],\"drivers\":[\"post-unwinding enrollment drift remains mildly negative\",\"updated vintage includes retroactive and late-processed enrollment\",\"March 2026 official level is much lower than older catalog prior\",\"state renewal operations and reporting methodology remain the main downside risk\",\"CHIP and child continuous-eligibility rules support the level\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/program-information/medicaid-and-chip-enrollment-data/report-highlights\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/methodology-about-medicaid-chip-enrollment-report\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-27T23:09:35Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast April 2026 CMS Medicaid and CHIP enrollment\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is the April 2026 national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment row in CMS monthly enrollment data, updated-data fixed vintage, converted from persons to millions. This is a national total, not a weighted average or a state row.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened Medicaid.gov March 2026 Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment Data Highlights.\",\"result\":\"Fetched March 2026 national Total Medicaid and CHIP Enrollment of 74,294,361 people, with Medicaid enrollment of 67,080,865 and CHIP enrollment of 7,213,496.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read the same official CMS highlights page for child-enrollment context and data timestamp.\",\"result\":\"Fetched March 2026 child Medicaid plus CHIP enrollment of 35,571,626, equal to 47.9% of total Medicaid and CHIP enrollment; the map/data note says March 2026 data were last updated June 26, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the Medicaid.gov monthly reports page for release availability and target timing.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official release list showing Preliminary March 2026 data last updated June 26, 2026; Updated February 2026 data last updated June 26, 2026; Updated January 2026 data last updated June 26, 2026; and no April 2026 entry visible as of this run.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened CMS methodology page for preliminary versus updated enrollment data.\",\"result\":\"Fetched methodology stating states report 2 data types, preliminary and updated; updated data is reported 1 month after close of the reporting period and includes retroactive enrollment and applications processed after month end.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the latest official level is 74.294 million in March 2026, and CMS's release list shows the comparable monthly files are updated monthly. I anchor April near March rather than the older catalog prior around 79 million because the current CMS highlight is the authoritative public series level.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and vintage split: March gives the level anchor; post-unwinding Medicaid/CHIP enrollment still appears to be drifting down, but by 2026 the extreme unwinding losses should be mostly over. The updated April vintage should be a little higher than a preliminary April print would be because updated data include retroactive and late-processed enrollment.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Policy-mechanism split: continuous eligibility for children, normal population growth, and retroactive processing support the level. Renewal redeterminations, income growth moving some adults out of eligibility, and state reporting cleanups pull down. I do not apply a large one-off shock because April 2026 is before any later community-engagement compliance pulse would affect enrollment mechanically.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point: start from the March official total 74.294361 million, subtract 0.20 million for continued post-unwinding attrition, add 0.06 million for updated-vintage retroactive/late processing, giving 74.154361 million, rounded to 74.15. Interval: with only one directly fetched current-series national total visible in the fast run and CMS noting methodology changes can affect comparability, use a wider 80% band of about -1.45/+1.45 million around the point, giving 72.70 to 75.60 million.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration and scenarios: downside outside the interval would require a broad state renewal or methodology drop below 72.7 million; upside outside the interval would require updated April data to include unusually large retroactive enrollment, state resubmissions, or a reporting-break rebound above 75.6 million. The central case is near-flat to mildly down from March.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":74.15,\"ciLow\":72.7,\"ciHigh\":75.6}]}"}}
