d-vintage retroactive/late processing, giving 74.154361 million, rounded to 74.15. Interval: with only one directly fetched current-series national total visible in the fast run and CMS noting methodology changes can affect comparability, use a wider 80% band of about -1.45/+1.45 million around the point, giving 72.70 to 75.60 million."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration and scenarios: downside outside the interval would require a broad state renewal or methodology drop below 72.7 million; upside outside the interval would require updated April data to include unusually large retroactive enrollment, state resubmissions, or a reporting-break rebound above 75.6 million. The central case is near-flat to mildly down from March."},{"kind":"forecast","point":74.15,"ciLow":72.7,"ciHigh":75.6}]}
